Hi all, <div>Thanks for Nimble - it looks like a really flexible tool.</div><div><br>I am learning Nimble by experimenting with implementing the &quot;Latent Slice Sampler&quot; of Li and Walker (<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.08509.pdf" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.08509.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476605663000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1k6_yLqg1ViMxThecolgXT">2010.08509.pdf (arxiv.org)</a>), specifically the very simple algorithm described in their paper&#39;s section 5 (Discussion).</div><div><br>I have code that seems to work on my baby test example, and runs (SLOWLY) in uncompiled form. However, when I try to compile it I get the following error:<br><font face="Courier New">Error in thisKeywordInfo$processor(code, nfProc) : <br>  object &#39;callerCode&#39; not found</font><br></div><div><font face="Courier New"><br></font></div><div>I read in the group that this may have something to do with runtime indexing by string, but I hacked together my sampler code from the Nimble&#39;s source for it&#39;s slice and block_RW samplers, and don&#39;t think I&#39;m doing anything that&#39;s not done there. Any help would be appreciated. Here is the full code:<br><br><font face="Courier New" size="2">sampler_latent_slice &lt;- nimbleFunction(<br>  name = &#39;sampler_latent_slice&#39;,<br>  contains = sampler_BASE,<br>  setup = function(model, mvSaved, target, control) {<br>    ## control list extraction<br>    scaleInit &lt;- extractControlElement(control,&#39;scaleInit&#39;,1)<br>    lambda &lt;- extractControlElement(control,&#39;lambda&#39;,0.1)<br>    tryMax &lt;- extractControlElement(control,&#39;tryMax&#39;,1000)<br>    <br>    ## node list generation <br>    targetAsScalar &lt;- model$expandNodeNames(target, returnScalarComponents = TRUE,)<br>    <br>    calcNodes &lt;- model$getDependencies(target)<br>    calcNodesNoSelf &lt;- model$getDependencies(target, self = FALSE)<br>    isStochCalcNodesNoSelf &lt;- model$isStoch(calcNodesNoSelf)   ## should be made faster<br>    calcNodesNoSelfDeterm &lt;- calcNodesNoSelf[!isStochCalcNodesNoSelf]<br>    calcNodesNoSelfStoch &lt;- calcNodesNoSelf[isStochCalcNodesNoSelf]<br>    <br>    # store dimension of targets<br>    targetDimension &lt;- length(targetAsScalar)<br>    cat(&quot;targetDimension &quot;, targetDimension,&quot;
&quot;)<br>  <br>    sPrev &lt;- rep(scaleInit,targetDimension)<br>    timesRan &lt;- 0<br>    tries &lt;- 0<br>  <br>    cat(&quot;done lss setup
&quot;)<br>  },<br>  run = function() {<br>    ### Li/Walker Step 1<br><br>    u &lt;- exp(model$getLogProb(calcNodes))<br>    w &lt;- u*runif(1,min=0,max=1)<br>    y0 &lt;- values(model,targetAsScalar) # I hope this works!<br>    l &lt;- runif(n=targetDimension,min=y0-sPrev/2,y0+sPrev/2)<br>    # hope this is persisted! <br>    sPrev &lt;&lt;- rexp(n=targetDimension, rate=lambda*sPrev)+ 2*abs(l-y0) # truncated exponential - to sample we just shift by the truncation threshold<br><br></font></div><div><font face="Courier New" size="2">    ## Li/Walker Step 2<br>    a &lt;- l - sPrev/2<br>    b &lt;- l + sPrev/2<br><br></font></div><div><font face="Courier New" size="2">    ## Li/Walker Step 3/4<br>    y_star &lt;- runif(targetDimension,min=a, max=b)<br>    tries &lt;&lt;- 1<br>    #  EVALUATE MODEL AT y_star<br>    lp &lt;- setAndCalculateTarget(y_star)<br>    while( !is.nan(lp) &amp; (exp(lp) &lt;w)  &amp; (tries &lt; tryMax) ){<br>      for(j in 1:targetDimension){<br>        if( y_star[[j]] &lt; y0[[j]]){<br>          a[[j]] &lt;- max(a[[j]],y_star[[j]])<br>        } else {<br>          b[[j]] &lt;- min(b[[j]],y_star[[j]])<br>        }<br>      }<br>      y_star &lt;- runif(targetDimension,min=a, max=b)<br>      tries &lt;&lt;- tries+1<br>      lp &lt;- setAndCalculateTarget(y_star)<br>  <br>    }<br>    <br>    if(tries == tryMax){<br>      cat(&quot;Warning: latent slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions &quot;, tryMax,&quot;
&quot;)<br>      nimCopy(from = mvSaved, to = model, row = 1, nodes = target, logProb = TRUE) # sk test<br>      nimCopy(from = mvSaved, to = model, row = 1, nodes = calcNodesNoSelfDeterm, logProb = FALSE)<br>      nimCopy(from = mvSaved, to = model, row = 1, nodes = calcNodesNoSelfStoch, logProbOnly = TRUE)<br>      <br>    } else {  # accept y_star<br>      nimCopy(from = model, to = mvSaved, row = 1, nodes = target, logProb = TRUE) # sk test<br>      nimCopy(from = model, to = mvSaved, row = 1, nodes = calcNodesNoSelfDeterm, logProb = FALSE)<br>      nimCopy(from = model, to = mvSaved, row = 1, nodes = calcNodesNoSelfStoch, logProbOnly = TRUE)<br>      <br>    }<br>    <br>  },<br>  methods = list(<br>    setAndCalculateTarget = function(valueVec = double(1)) {<br>      values(model,target) &lt;&lt;- valueVec<br>      lp &lt;- model$calculate(target)<br>      #lp &lt;- model$calculate(targetAsScalar)<br>      if(lp == -Inf) return(-Inf) <br>      lp &lt;- lp + model$calculate(calcNodesNoSelf)<br>      returnType(double())<br>      return(lp)<br>    },<br>    reset = function() {<br>     <br>      timesRan     &lt;&lt;- 0<br>      tries &lt;&lt;- 0<br>   <br>    }<br>  )<br>)<br><br><br><br><br>simpleCode&lt;- nimbleCode({<br>  for(i in 1:100){<br>    gg[i] ~ dnorm(mean=0,sd=1)<br>  }<br>})<br>simpleModel &lt;- nimbleModel(code=simpleCode, name=&quot;simp&quot;, constants=list(), <br>                           data=list(),<br>                           inits = list(gg=rep(0,100)))<br>simpleConf &lt;- configureMCMC(simpleModel,monitors=&quot;gg&quot;,print = TRUE)<br>simpleConf$removeSampler(&quot;gg&quot;)<br>simpleConf$addSampler(&quot;gg[1:100]&quot;,type=&quot;sampler_latent_slice&quot;)<br>simpleConf$printSamplers()<br>CsimpleModel &lt;- compileNimble(simpleModel,showCompilerOutput=TRUE)<br>simpleMCMC &lt;- buildMCMC(simpleConf)<br>CsimpleMCMC &lt;- compileNimble(simpleMCMC, project = simpleModel,<br>                             resetFunctions = TRUE, showCompilerOutput = TRUE)<br>simpleSamples &lt;- runMCMC(mcmc=simpleMCMC,<br>                         niter=5000,<br>                         #nburnin = 10000, <br>                         #thin=100,<br>                         nchains = 1, <br>                         progressBar = T <br>)<br></font><br></div>
